The identity $\mathop{\text{lcm}}[a,b]\cdot \gcd(a,b)=ab$ holds for all positive integers $a$ and $b$.

Let $a=315$ in this identity, and let $b$ be the number we're looking for. Thus $$7!\cdot 9 = 315\cdot b,$$so $$b = \frac{7!\cdot 9}{315} = \frac{7!\cdot 9}{35\cdot 9} = \frac{7!}{35} = \frac{\cancel{7}\cdot 6\cdot \cancel{5}\cdot 4\cdot 3\cdot 2\cdot 1}{\cancel{35}} = 6\cdot4\cdot3\cdot2 = 144.$$

\boxed{144}

